{"key":"enterprise/T1132.001","id":"T1132.001","name":"Standard Encoding","domain":"enterprise","level":"subtechnique","parent_id":"T1132","tactics":["command-and-control"],"platforms":["ESXi","Linux","macOS","Windows"],"environments":["cloud-hosted-endpoint","onprem","virtualization"],"environment_basis":"project_taxonomy_from_upstream_platforms","summary":"Adversaries may encode data with a standard data encoding system to make the content of command and control traffic more difficult to detect. Command and control (C2) information can be encoded using a standard data encoding system that adheres to existing protocol specifications. Common data encoding schemes include ASCII, Unicode, hexadecimal, Base64, and MIME. Some data encoding systems may also result in data compression, such as gzip.","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1132/001","source_stix_id":"attack-pattern--04fd5427-79c7-44ea-ae13-11b24778ff1c","source_modified":"2026-05-12T15:12:00.620Z","source_object_version":"1.1","telemetry":{"status":"mapped","components":[{"id":"DC0038","name":"Application Log Content","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0038","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--9c2fa0ae-7abc-485a-97f6-699e3b6cf9fa","page":"telemetry/DC0038/"},{"id":"DC0082","name":"Network Connection Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0082","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--181a9f8c-c780-4f1f-91a8-edb770e904ba","page":"telemetry/DC0082/"},{"id":"DC0085","name":"Network Traffic Content","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0085","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--3772e279-27d6-477a-9fe3-c6beb363594c","page":"telemetry/DC0085/"},{"id":"DC0078","name":"Network Traffic Flow","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0078","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--a7f22107-02e5-4982-9067-6625d4a1765a","page":"telemetry/DC0078/"},{"id":"DC0032","name":"Process Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0032","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--3d20385b-24ef-40e1-9f56-f39750379077","page":"telemetry/DC0032/"},{"id":"DC0029","name":"Script Execution","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0029","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--9f387817-df83-432a-b56b-a8fb7f71eedd","page":"telemetry/DC0029/"}],"strategies":[{"id":"DET0124","name":"Behavior-chain detection for T1132.001 Data Encoding: Standard Encoding (Base64/Hex/MIME) across Windows, Linux, macOS, ESXi","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0124","stix_id":"x-mitre-detection-strategy--1f6a450a-fd29-4e5c-9708-1ae4616c28c3","relationship_id":"relationship--0509ff0b-2095-466f-a6a4-72640f9a77fb"}],"analytics":[{"id":"AN0345","name":"Analytic 0345","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0124#AN0345","guidance":"Process invokes a standard encoder (e.g., PowerShell -enc, certutil -encode, base64 via .NET/Invoke-Expression) or emits long Base64/hex literals → shortly followed by outbound network egress with high bytes_out:bytes_in ratio or HTTP headers/payloads containing Base64/MIME blocks.","platforms":["Windows"],"strategy_id":"DET0124"},{"id":"AN0346","name":"Analytic 0346","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0124#AN0346","guidance":"Shell/utility (base64, xxd -p, od, openssl enc -base64, python/perl base64 libraries) encodes data → subsequent outbound connections (curl/wget/bash TCP, socat, python requests) with high asymmetry or Base64/MIME blobs in HTTP/DNS payloads.","platforms":["Linux"],"strategy_id":"DET0124"},{"id":"AN0347","name":"Analytic 0347","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0124#AN0347","guidance":"Processes use base64/xxd/openssl/python Objective‑C APIs to encode data (seen in EndpointSecurity exec events or Unified Logs) → quick outbound connections with large bytes_out or HTTP POSTs carrying Base64/MIME bodies.","platforms":["macOS"],"strategy_id":"DET0124"},{"id":"AN0348","name":"Analytic 0348","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0124